JtTW1LCXjPFDeRBRjur", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and it's healthy again. But opening the incident created a duplicate, and both copies paged the on-call engineer.\n\n**Rollback (done and verified)**\n- checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- Both v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) are marked unhealthy, so the most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n- After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident (SEV2 opened, but there's a duplicate)**\n- My first request to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list, it showed nothing, so I sent the request again. That created INC-0002.\n- A later check showed the first request had actually gone through as INC-0001. The list just hadn't shown it yet.\n- So there are now two identical open SEV2 incidents for checkout-api. Each one describes the failure, the rollback to v2.3.0, the recovery, and a follow-up to find the cause before redeploying v2.3.1.\n- I can't close or merge incidents, so someone will need to close INC-0002 as a duplicate of INC-0001. It's worth telling the on-call engineer that the second page was the same issue.", "type": "text"}]}]}